size-buffers: fluid model in 10 us steps. Illustrative, not a measurement.
stack             dpdk
arrival           idle 0.000 Mpps, burst 10.000 Mpps for 3000 us from 200 us
stage 1           RX ring: 1024 packets, drained at 14.000 Mpps
stage 2           mempool and application queue: 2048 packets, read at 6.000 Mpps
reader pause      none

dropped, stage 1  0 packets (imissed)
dropped, stage 2  9952 packets (rx_nombuf, then imissed)
first drop        stage 2 at 710 us
peak fill         stage 1: 0 of 1024, stage 2: 2048 of 2048

To lose nothing in this scenario:
ring              0 packets, 0 KiB per queue at 2048 B
stage 2           12000 packets
ring memory now   2048 KiB per queue, 2048 KiB for 1 queue(s)
